dsv41 patch 0059 (20.10.2026): NVFP4 KV records on GB10. In the image, off: rejected at the KV-KLD gate (see below).
Base: the v7 files (0057). 0061 is the mixed variant (FP8 sliding window, NVFP4 only for the compressed KV).
Why: the KV is DeepSeek's fp8_ds_mla record (448 FP8 NoPE dims + 64 BF16 RoPE dims + UE8M0 scales = 584 B per state).
DeepSeek's DeepInfer release (Apache-2.0, SM100/Ascend only) uses FP4 (288 B) for the main KV. FlashInfer in the image
already has SM120 sparse-MLA kernels for a 384 B NVFP4 record (448 NoPE values as e2m1 with an e4m3 scale per 16, 64 RoPE
values BF16; page = 64 x 352 B data + 64 x 32 B scales), but vLLM never used it on GB10.
How: VLLM_DSV41_KV_NVFP4=1 stores the sliding-window and the compressed caches in that record (384 B, pages aligned to
512 B; the FP8 indexer pages are aligned to 512 B as well). Writing: RoPE in BF16 (a plain-row op for q + kv, a Triton
RoPE for the compressor / context path), then FlashInfer's own nvfp4_quantize_append_sparse_mla_cache, so writer and
reader match by construction; reading: kv_cache_format="nvfp4". The indexer stays FP8. DSpark's verify is non-causal,
which makes the SWA index width cdiv(128 window + 5 drafts, 64) x 64 = 192; the NVFP4 kernels take 128 or 512 only, so
the SWA indices are padded with -1 to 512 (entries beyond swa_topk_lens are never read). Our Triton verify kernel (0022)
is switched off with NVFP4 records.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz, image v9, 3.75 GiB KV pool per node, one window against FP8 with 0057):
KV pool 1,346,928 -> 2,013,868 tokens (+49.5 %; the offline harness with the real allocator code predicted 2,013,561),
bytes per token live (250K-token prompt) 2,187 -> 1,574, cost per verify round -0.92 % (geometric mean), needles at 250K
6/6, but KV-KLD (teacher-forced prompt logprobs, 44K positions, top-5) KL 0.0280 / top-1 95.0 % against FP8 records;
first 127 positions KL 0.147 prose / 0.094 code, 128-4K 0.032 / 0.017, > 4K 0.029 / 0.015. The run-to-run floor of this
measurement (two identical requests, FP8) is KL ~0.008 / top-1 ~97.5 % from position 128 on (bit-identical before), so
the NVFP4 records add ~0.02, about as much as the whole weight quantization (KLD 0.0201 against the native weights).
Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_KV_NVFP4=1 (default 0 = off).
